那么让我先列举一些推论，然后简要过一遍为什么它们成立。我们首先从以下内容开始：设 W 为子空间——这里我沿用刚才回顾中的记号，
So let me just start by listing some consequences, and we'll just run through briefly why those things are true. So let's just start with the following: so let W be the subspace—so I'm just going to retain

7
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:50,749
设 W 为由集合 {v_1, ..., v_n} 所张成的子空间。回顾上次我们讲过，“张成”（span）意味着由特定向量集合构成的所有线性组合。
notation from the recall here, and I'm going to let W be the subspace spanned by the set v_1 through v_n. Now recall we saw last time the word span means the set of things which are linear combinations of a particular set of vectors.

8
00:02:50,749 --> 00:03:00,940
因此 W 是所有形如 c_1 v_1 + ... + c_n v_n 的元素，其中 c_1到 c_n 取遍这里的隐式域 F。
So W is all things of the form c_1 v_1 plus dot dot dot c_n v_n, as c_1 through c_n range over the implicit field here, F.

9
00:03:00,940 --> 00:03:22,934
背后的前提是 V 是域 F 上的向量空间，F 为某个域，通常来说将这个域看作实数域 R 就足够了，但这并非总是成立；有限域有奇特的性质，大家要牢记在心，尤其当你将有限向量集合相加时。
So running behind the scenes here is that V is over F, F being some field, and in general it suffices to think of this field as being R, but that's not always true; finite fields have weird properties, so you should bear that in mind, especially when you're adding finite sets of vectors.

10
00:03:22,934 --> 00:03:27,348
不过目前我们只关注这些一般性结论。
But for now we're just concerned with these sorts of general results.

11
00:03:27,348 --> 00:03:54,333
好的，设 W' 为由其余向量 v_{n+1} 到 v_m 张成的子空间。那么有以下两个推论：首先，它们的交集是零空间。
Okay, so and let W' be the subspace spanned by the remaining vectors v_{n+1} through v_m. Well then, here are two consequences: then first of all, the intersection of these things is zero.

12
00:03:54,333 --> 00:04:17,938
但这并不算主要结论；重点在于我接下来要写下的内容，它充分利用了这一事实，即：我们有一个线性同构，存在于 W 与 W' 的直积之间。
But that's not really a major result; the point is more the thing that I'm about to write down, which sort of takes advantage of that fact, which is: and we have a linear isomorphism between the product of W and W'.

13
00:04:17,938 --> 00:04:39,699
什么是直积？这是上一章某一节阅读材料中的内容，不过为了帮大家重温一下：这是有序对 (w, w') 的集合，其中 w 取遍 W，小写 w 取遍大写 W，小写 w'取遍大写 W'。
What's the product? Well, this was part of the reading for one of the sections in the last chapter, but just to refresh your memories, this is the set of ordered pairs (w, w'), where w ranges over W, little w ranges over big W, and little w' ranges over big W'.

14
00:04:39,699 --> 00:04:56,371
在这个直积空间与 V 之间存在一个线性同构，即取有序对 (w, w') 并映为其和：(w, w') ↦ w + w'。
There's a linear isomorphism between this product thing and V, where we just take a pair (w, w') and we map it to its sum.

15
00:04:56,371 --> 00:05:16,919
那么利用上次引入的术语，谁能直观地说明为什么 W 与 W' 的交集仅仅是零向量空间？
So using a term introduced last time, can somebody give me a way of seeing fairly immediately that the intersection of W and W' is just the zero vector space?

16
00:05:17,999 --> 00:05:33,200
对。是的，那确实，对，与张成有关，但有一个关键得多的因素。你立刻用到的其实是线性无关性。
Yes. Yes, so that would be sort of, yeah, it has to do with spanning, but there's a much more critical thing. The thing that you really use immediately is linear independence.

17
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:46,035
因此它直接由这两组向量之间广义的线性无关性得出，具体来说，即这两个集合合在一起是线性无关的。为什么呢？
So it follows immediately from a sort of generalized notion of linear independence between these two things, specifically the fact that the accumulation of these two sets is linearly independent. Well, why?

18
00:05:46,035 --> 00:06:10,214
假设有一个元素属于 W，那么根据张成的定义，我显然可以将其写作 a_1 v_1 + ... + a_n v_n；如果有 w' ∈ W'，我可以将其写作 a_{n+1} v_{n+1}一直到 a_m v_m。
I mean, suppose I have something which is in W, well, I can certainly write it by definition of span as a_1 v_1 through a_n v_n, and if I have w' in W', I can write that as a_{n+1} v_{n+1} up to a_m v_m.

19
00:06:10,214 --> 00:06:22,479
这些就是 W 与 W' 的一般元素，如果它们相等，如果它们相等，那么我可以相减得到 w - w' = 0，
So these are just sort of general elements of W and W', and if these things are equal, so if I have these things being equal,

20
00:06:22,479 --> 00:06:49,333
但这就是形如a_1 v_1 + ... + a_n v_n - (a_{n+1} v_{n+1} + ... + a_m v_m) 的线性组合——直接取负——这一项等于零。
well then I can subtract them, so w - w' is zero, but that's this sort of non-trivial linear combination of a_1 v_1 up to a_n v_n plus minus a_{n+1} v_{n+1} up through a_m v_m—so just negate that—this thing equals zero.

21
00:06:49,333 --> 00:07:07,200
既然 W——抱歉，黑板这里写的应该是 v：v_1 到 v_n，v_{n+1} 到 v_m；v_1 到 v_n，v_{n+1} 到 v_m——
And since W—sorry, these should be v's over here: v_1 to v_n, v_{n+1} to v_m; v_1 to v_n, v_{n+1} to v_m—well, since these things are all linearly

22
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:24,779
既然这些向量全都是根据假设线性无关的——它们构成了一组基——所有这些 a_i 都是零，因此每个 a_i 必为零，我们最初所取的元素必然是零。
independent by hypothesis—these things form a basis—all of these a_i's are zero, so each a_i must be zero, so the things that we started with must have been zero.

23
00:07:24,779 --> 00:07:38,107
因此正是线性无关性以完全本质的方式告诉我们：这类由线性无关集张成出的子空间的交集必为零。
So it's the linear independence which is telling us in like a completely essential way that the intersection of these sorts of linearly independent spans must be zero.

24
00:07:38,107 --> 00:07:56,960
现在我们来看它是一个线性同构的事实。至于它本身是个同态，几乎直接源自直积上向量空间结构的定义。在直积中如何做加法？
Now let's move on to the fact that this thing is a linear isomorphism. Well, the fact that it's just a homomorphism follows pretty much immediately from the definition of vector space structure on the product. So how do you add things in here?

25
00:07:56,960 --> 00:08:11,505
按分量相加：如果有 (w_1, w_1') 与 (w_2, w_2')，直接相加得 (w_1 + w_2, w_1' + w_2')。
Well, you add them componentwise: so if I have (w_1, w_1') and (w_2, w_2'), you just add these things: (w_1 + w_2, w_1' + w_2').

26
00:08:11,505 --> 00:08:28,464
如果我乘上标量，c * (w, w')，结果就是 (c w, c w')。因此显而易见，这里的映射至少必须是一个线性变换。
And if I multiply by a scalar, c * (w, w'), that's just (c w, c w'). So it's pretty apparent that this map here must at the very least be a linear transformation.

27
00:08:28,464 --> 00:08:40,160
大家都清楚了吗？
So is that pretty clear to everyone?

28
00:08:40,160 --> 00:08:51,738
好的，一句话概括满射性：满射性来自哪里？
Okay, the surjectivity in a word: where does the surjectivity come from?

29
00:08:51,738 --> 00:09:01,240
张成，没错！来自 v_1 到 v_m 张成全空间的事实。
Spanning, exactly! The fact that v_1 up through v_m spans.

30
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:18,920
因为 V 中的每个元素按定义都是 v_1 到 v_m 的线性组合，所以我取线性组合的第一部分来自 W，第二部分来自 W'，将它们相加，就得到了 V 中我想要的任何向量。
Because, you know, everything in V is by definition some linear combination of v_1 through v_m, and so I take, you know, the first part of the linear combination from W and the second part of the linear combination from W', I add those up and I get whatever vector I wanted in V.

31
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:31,600
因此满射性源自张成。最后是单射性：这来自哪里？对，正是线性无关性。
So the surjectivity follows from spanning. And then finally injectivity: where does that come from? Yes, linear independence, exactly.

32
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:53,131
事实上我们已经证明了线性无关性最关键的结论，具体来说就是 W 与 W' 的交集为零。因为假设我有 w_1 + w_1'等于 w_2 + w_2'，对吧？
In fact, we've already shown the critical thing about linear independence, which is specifically that the intersection of W and W' is zero. Because if I have, you know, suppose I have w_1 + w_1' equaling w_2 + w_2', right?

33
00:09:53,131 --> 00:09:57,939
这蕴含了 w_1 - w_2 = w_2' - w_1'。
Well, this implies that w_1 - w_2 is equal to w_2' - w_1'.

34
00:09:57,939 --> 00:10:12,757
这项属于 W，那项属于 W'，因此无论这个公共向量是什么，它都属于 W ∩ W'，而交集是零。
This thing is in W, this thing is in W', so whatever this common vector is, it's in the intersection of W and W', which is zero.

35
00:10:12,757 --> 00:10:28,120
但如果这项是零，且那项也是零，这就蕴含了 w_1 = w_2 且 w_2' = w_1'，因此我们最初将这些元素写成和式的方式是唯一的。
But if this thing is zero and this thing is zero, that implies that w_1 equals w_2 and w_2' equals w_1', so the way we wrote these things as sums to start with was unique.

36
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:35,560
这很清楚吧？关于这里有什么问题吗？
Is that pretty clear? Are there any questions about this?

37
00:10:41,040 --> 00:10:50,529
很好。第二个推论：现在让我们先抛开刚才引入的记号。
Great. Second consequence: so now let's sort of forget about the sort of notation we introduced before.

38
00:10:50,529 --> 00:11:00,269
我们仍然从同一个向量空间V 出发，但不再按刚才的方式定义 W；我们只设 W 为任意子空间。
So we're just going to start with, you know, maybe the same vector space V, but we're not going to have W defined as before; we're just going to let W be some subspace.

39
00:11:00,269 --> 00:11:55,760
如果 W 是V 的子空间，那么存在另一个子空间，存在 V 的另一个子空间 W'，使得复合映射——我显然可以把 W' 嵌入到 V 中，只需让 w' 映为 w'，我是说，这也就是嵌入映射，相当于 W' 上的恒等映射；
So if W is a subspace of V, then there is another subspace, and there's another subspace W' of V, such that the composite map—so I can certainly just inject W' into V by just letting w' map to w', I mean, this is just sort of the the embedding map, this is sort of the identity map on W',

40
00:11:55,760 --> 00:12:41,360
并且回忆一下还有一个正则映射，它是一个满射，有一个正则商映射，它将这个 w' 映为 w' 的陪集，即 w' 所在的 W-陪集w' + W，使得这个复合映射是一个同构。这是一个极好的结论。
and recall also that there is a canonical map and it's a surjection, there's a canonical quotient map, so canonical quotient map which just takes this W' and maps it to the coset of W', the W-coset of W' Prime, such that this composite map is an isomorphism. So this is a great result.

41
00:12:41,360 --> 00:13:03,236
这就是上一讲结尾处所提到的那个结果，在上一讲中给出了一个反例，即由一个群论的、一般群论反例（涉及我们上周讲过的循环群）说明一般群中并不成立。
It's this is this is the result that was referred to at the very end of last lecture, and for which there was a sort of counterexample given, or part of which there was a counterexample given to by a group-theoretic general group-theoretic example involving the cyclic groups that we saw last week.

42
00:13:03,236 --> 00:13:23,240
但事实证明向量空间性质足够优良，事情总是能以如此完美的方式分解；我会在第三个推论中进一步阐明这一点。但有人能简要给出这个结论的证明思路吗？好的，艾米莉。
But it turns out that vector spaces are nice enough that things sort of always break up in this great way, and I'll elucidate that further with a third consequence. But can anybody just give me very briefly the argument for this?

43
00:13:30,840 --> 00:14:14,753
完全正确。意译一下：要点在于我们取 W 的一组基 v_1 到 v_n，将其扩充为V 的一组基——我们完全可以这样做——然后像之前一样令 W' 为——抱歉，这里应该是 v_1 到 v_m——v_{n+1} 到 v_m 的张成。
Exactly. So paraphrasing: the point is that we take a basis, well, v_1 through v_n of W, extend to basis v_1, ..., v_n, v_{n+1} up through v_m of V—we're allowed to do this—then we just let W' be as before the span of—sorry, this should be v_1 up through v_m— span of v_{n+1} up through v_m.

44
00:14:14,753 --> 00:14:29,475
接下来不难验证它恰好具有所需的性质。首先，它显然是一个同态。
And then it's not so hard to verify that this has exactly the right property. The thing is, well, certainly a homomorphism.

45
00:14:29,475 --> 00:14:43,616
我是说，它是一个变换直接由定义得出；我们选择的映射就是线性变换，而线性变换的复合依然是线性变换。
I mean that it's a transformation follows just immediately by the definition; we chose these things to be linear transformations, and the composite of a linear transformation is a linear transformation.

46
00:14:43,616 --> 00:14:55,960
满射性则源于我们之前看到的：V 中的任何元素都可以写成 W' 中元素与 W 中元素的和。
The surjectivity follows from the fact that we saw before that everything in V can be written as a sum of something in W' and something in W.

47
00:14:55,960 --> 00:15:19,907
因此如果我们在商空间 V/W 中取一个元素，我可以将其提升到 V 中，写成形如w + w' 的形式，其中 w ∈ W 且 w' ∈ W'，那么陪集 w' + W必然就是我们最初所取的陪集。
So if we take some element of V/W, then I can lift it to something in V, write it as something of the form w + w', where w is in W and w' is in W', and then certainly the coset w' plus big W must be the coset we started out with.

48
00:15:19,907 --> 00:15:34,477
这很清楚吧？所以满射性直接由陪集的定义和张成得出。
Is that pretty clear? So surjectivity is straightforward from definition of cosets and the spanning.

49
00:15:34,477 --> 00:15:46,439
因此在这类结论中，每当你需要证明满射时，就考虑张成；每当你需要证明单射时，就考虑线性无关。
So in general in these sorts of results, whenever you see something that you need to be surjective, think about spanning; whenever you need something to be injective, think about linear independence.

50
00:15:46,439 --> 00:15:57,920
这些是通用的诀窍，并且这必然是由上次结论推导出的所有推论中的基本论证。
These are just sort of general tips and tricks, and this is certainly going to be the basic argument in all the consequences of the result from last time that we started with.

51
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:07,160
至于单射性：同样，这属于线性无关类的论证。
And so injectivity: well, again this is a sort of linear independence type result.

52
00:16:07,160 --> 00:16:19,067
如果我有——我们刚才看到，显然可以把任意陪集写成 w' + W 的形式，其中 w'属于大写的 W'。
So if I have—I mean I can certainly, we just saw I can certainly write any coset in the form w' plus W, where w' Prime is in big W'.

53
00:16:19,067 --> 00:16:30,329
假设有两个元素具有相同的像，那么我们已经看到 w_1' - w_2'必属于 W。
And so suppose I have two things which have the same image, well then we've seen that w_1' minus w_2' must be in W.

54
00:16:30,329 --> 00:16:57,518
于是这个元素属于 W，但它同时也属于 W'，再次利用前面的线性无关性论证，它必然为零，所以它们必须是同一个陪集。很好，让我们来看结合了前两个推论的第三个推论。
So we have this thing which is in W, but it's also in W', and then again by the same linear independence argument we saw before, this thing must be zero, so these must be the same coset. Great, so let's look at a third consequence that brings together the first two consequences I've listed here.

55
00:16:57,518 --> 00:17:18,780
请问。（那是大写……？）这两个都是大写的W。
Yes, go ahead. (Is that capital...?) So these are both capital W's.

56
00:17:18,780 --> 00:17:59,560
第三点是，如果我们把推论 1 和 2 结合起来，把推论 1 和 2 的论证结合在一起，我们就得到对 V 的任意子空间 W（设 W 是 V 的子空间），在 V 与 W 及其商空间的直积之间存在同构，即 V同构于 W × (V/W)。
So the third thing is that if we put 1 and 2 together, put the arguments for 1 and 2 together, we get that for any subspace W of V (suppose we have W subspace of V), there's an isomorphism between V and W with its product with the quotient, so V is isomorphic to W cross V/W.

57
00:17:59,560 --> 00:18:12,194
这可以作为一个小练习——不用交作业，但在课后复习笔记时思考一下为什么这两点合起来能给出这个结论。
And it's just a sort of exercise—I mean, don't hand this in or anything, but think about when you're reading over your notes why these two things come together to give this result.

58
00:18:12,194 --> 00:18:21,142
这是一个非常漂亮的结果；它准确地告诉你如何理解向量空间中的商空间。
But it's just a very sort of cute result; it tells you exactly how to think about quotients and so on in the case of vector spaces.

59
00:18:21,142 --> 00:18:39,255
切莫被误导：一般群中的商群结构可能极其复杂、极其困难；但在向量空间的情形下，把商空间理解为某种补空间是非常简单的。
Don't be fooled: I mean in general in groups, quotient structures can be very, very complicated, very, very difficult; but in the case of vector spaces, it's very, very easy to understand quotients as being sort of complements.

60
00:18:39,255 --> 00:18:55,959
第四个结论——在讲第四个结论之前，有人能根据这个结果告诉我关于 V、W 以及 V/W 的维数关系吗？
And a fourth result—well actually, before I move on to a fourth result, can somebody tell me something as a result of this about the dimensions of V, W, and V/W?

61
00:18:55,959 --> 00:19:11,543
对，……的维数。没错：V 的维数必然等于 W 的维数加上 V/W 的维数：dim V = dim W + dim(V/W)。
Yes, dimension of... Yes, exactly: the dimension of V must be equal to the dimension of W plus the dimension of V mod W.

62
00:19:11,543 --> 00:20:00,234
现在让我们把这个结论应用到一般的线性映射上：对一般的线性映射：如果 f: V → U 是一个线性变换，那么有两点成立：首先，V 同构于 ker(f) 与im(f) 的直积；
Now let's use this result on a general linear map. So on a general linear map: so if f: V -> U is a linear transformation, then, well, two things are true: first of all, V is isomorphic to the product of the kernel of f

63
00:20:00,234 --> 00:20:24,709
其次，再次由这里的论证，V 的维数等于 ker(f) 的维数加上im(f) 的维数：dim V = dim ker(f) + dim im(f)。
with the image of f, and consequently, again by the same argument as here, the dimension of V is equal to the dimension of the kernel of f plus the dimension of the image of f.

64
00:20:24,709 --> 00:20:37,960
什么群论定理蕴含了这一点？
What group-theoretic result implies this?

65
00:20:48,880 --> 00:20:59,184
对，确实，如果你面对的是有限群，比如如果这是有限域上的向量空间，并且我们有有限维向量空间，那确实成立。
Yes, true, so that would be true if you had like finite groups, like say if this were over a finite field we had a finite-dimensional vector space.

66
00:20:59,184 --> 00:21:05,026
你刚才说的是指我们讲过的计数公式，但我们当初是如何证明那个计数公式的？
So what you were saying, you're referring to the counting formula that we looked at, but how did we prove that particular counting formula?

67
00:21:05,026 --> 00:21:09,530
我们学过一个特定的定理。对，就是同构定理！
There was a particular theorem that we saw. Yeah, there was the isomorphism theorem!

68
00:21:09,530 --> 00:21:36,400
所以我们之前见过的关键结论——并且再怎么强调这个结论的重要性都不为过，因为正如我们这里的讨论彻底指导了我们理解向量空间的方式一样，几节课前讲过的同构定理彻底指导了我们分解群并理解其结构的方式。
So the key result that we previously saw—and this is, it can't be emphasized how important this result is, because in much the same way that our discussion here is completely informing the way we understand vector spaces, the isomorphism theorem we saw a few lectures ago completely informs the way we sort of decompose groups and understand their structure.

69
00:21:38,738 --> 00:21:45,360
因此我们学过一个极其重要的同构定理。为什么？
So we saw a very significant isomorphism theorem. So why?

70
00:21:45,360 --> 00:22:04,089
群的同构定理蕴含了向量空间的另一种同构定理，这里你只需额外加上线性结构，而这在一般群中是不具备的。
Well, the isomorphism theorem for groups implies another sort of isomorphism theorem for vector spaces, where you just sort of add in the linear structure, which is something that's lacking in general groups.

71
00:22:04,089 --> 00:22:31,120
但可以这样表述：如果我有一个同态——事实上在我们的情形下是线性变换，因为我们要保持线性结构，这里处理的是向量空间——因此给定向量空间 V 到 U 的线性变换，映射 f-bar——还记得我们讲过的诱导映射吗—
But here's a way of putting it: if I have a homomorphism—in fact in our case a linear transformation, because we want to preserve linear structure here, we're dealing with vector spaces—so given a linear transformation from some vector spaces V to U, the map f-bar—remember we talked about the induced map—

72
00:22:31,120 --> 00:23:10,049
—从 V模 ker(f) 映到 im(f) 的诱导映射：我们将 v + ker(f)——V 模子群的典型元素是v 加上该子群——映为 f(v)，这是像子群（在我们这里是子空间）中的良定义元素。
the induced map from V modulo the kernel of f going to the image of f, where we take v plus the kernel of f—a typical element of V modulo a subgroup is v plus that subgroup—so we take this and we map it to f(v), which is a well-defined element of the image subgroup, or in our case subspace.

73
00:23:10,049 --> 00:23:17,491
大家对这个熟悉吗？大家都还记得同构定理吗？这是非常重要的结论。
Is this familiar to everyone? Does everybody remember the isomorphism theorem? It's very important result.

74
00:23:17,491 --> 00:23:34,192
事实上如果你不记得了，我再怎么强调都不为过：回家在不翻书的情况下尝试自己把它证明出来是非常好的做法，它极其重要。
In fact if you don't remember it, I mean I can't emphasize enough, it's a really great idea to go home and try to figure out how to prove it without looking at the book, it's very important.

75
00:23:34,192 --> 00:23:41,480
关键在于这个映射是一个良定义的线性同构。
So the point is that this thing is a well-defined linear isomorphism.

76
00:23:41,480 --> 00:24:07,880
我们在群论情形中见过：我们看到它是一个良定义的同态，并且由陪集的基本性质，它是单射和满射。因此这里唯一新增的内容就是线性部分，而这仅涉及数乘：你只需验证这个映射保持数乘即可，这并不难。
I mean we saw this in the case of groups: we saw that this thing is a well-defined homomorphism, and that it's injective and surjective by sort of basic properties of cosets, and so the only thing that's sort of being added here is the linear part, and that just involves multiplication by scalars: you just have to see that this map preserves multiplication by scalars, and this isn't hard.

77
00:24:07,880 --> 00:24:27,487
于是有了这个结论，我们只需令 W 为 f 的核ker(f)，然后代入刚才的结果即可，因为这表明 V 同构于 ker(f) × im(f)，
So given this result, all we have to do is take W to be the kernel of f, and then just put it in this result, because this is saying that V is isomorphic to kernel of f times image of f,

78
00:24:27,487 --> 00:24:52,786
而这里是说 W ×(V/W)，但这里的 W 是核，V/W 是 V 模去核，正如我们刚才所见，那正是像空间，所以就是核乘上像空间。
and this is saying that, well, W times V/W, but W is the kernel here, V/W is V modulo the kernel, but that is, as we've just seen, the image, so kernel times image.

79
00:24:52,786 --> 00:24:58,303
到目前为止有什么问题吗？（所以实际上就是复合？）没错！
Any questions so far? (So really just composition?) Exactly!

80
00:24:58,303 --> 00:25:10,901
我们只是把这两个同构复合起来，把我们已知的所有事实综合起来，把这些同构结合起来，看看能发现群的什么结构。
We're taking just a composition of the two isomorphisms, we're putting together all the things we know, we're accumulating them, we're putting together the isomorphisms and we're seeing what we can find about the structure of the group.

81
00:25:10,901 --> 00:25:19,850
一般来说，如果你试图理解一般群的结构（对向量空间尤其如此），尝试各种映射是非常好的思路。
Now in general, it's a very good idea, if you're trying to understand the structure of a general group (and this is especially true of vector spaces), to try out various maps.

82
00:25:19,850 --> 00:25:22,520
映射赋予了你结构。
Maps are giving you the structure.

83
00:25:22,520 --> 00:25:41,840
这类定理告诉你：你可以利用通过各种方式定义的同态，来确定你最初研究的向量空间的大量结构；它们允许你分解映射等等，分解向量空间等等。
These sorts of theorems are telling you that you can take advantage of homomorphisms that you can define by various means to determine a lot about the structure of the vector spaces you started off with; they allow you to decompose maps and so on, decompose the vector spaces and so on.

84
00:25:41,840 --> 00:26:03,799
在群论中也是如此：你往往可以找到群之间的某种同态，从而帮助你将群分解为更简单的结构。好的，让我们来看一些稍微不同的内容。
This is very, very true in the case of groups: you often can find some sort of homomorphism between groups and allow this to help you decompose the group into simpler structure. Okay, let's move on to something a little different.

85
00:26:03,799 --> 00:26:32,479
这是关于群的另一类一般问题：如果我有群G 与 G' 之间的同态，比如说我们想要找出该同态的核与像。
So here's another sort of general problem for groups: well, if I have a homomorphism between groups G and G', say, we want to find the kernel and the image of this homomorphism.

86
00:26:32,479 --> 00:26:35,759
这是一类普遍问题，是你理所当然想要能够做到的事情。
Sort of a general problem, it's a sort of obvious thing that you want to be able to do.

87
00:26:35,759 --> 00:26:58,240
但一般而言这极其困难；事实上，这是能够利用我们这里所讨论结论的先决条件，但对于一般群来说，这可能非常、非常困难；一般群中通常很难。
Now this is in general very difficult; I mean in fact this is a sort of prerequisite for being able to take advantage of the kind of result that we're talking about here, but this can be very, very difficult in the case of general groups, this is generally difficult.

88
00:26:58,240 --> 00:27:03,960
但对于向量空间，这很容易！
But with vector spaces, it's easy!

89
00:27:06,800 --> 00:27:25,077
好的，容易的主要原因在于我们有基，因此我们可以把对象写成矩阵形式，并且我们有非常优秀的算法，比如行化简（初等行变换），帮助我们求解列空间等内容。
Okay, and the main reason it's easy is because we have bases, and hence we can write things in matrix form, and we have all these great algorithms like row reduction to help us find things like column spaces.

90
00:27:25,077 --> 00:27:48,308
因此本节课接下来的时间里，我将讨论如何在这类抽象向量空间与矩阵语言之间建立翻译，然后利用大家在初等线性代数中学到的所有矩阵算法，再提升回这些抽象向量空间中，从而解决这类问题。
So what I'm going to talk about for the rest of the lecture is how we make a translation between these sorts of abstract vector spaces and the language of matrices, and then use all those matrix algorithms that you learned in basic linear algebra to then lift back to these abstract vector spaces so that you can solve problems like this.

91
00:27:48,308 --> 00:28:20,383
所以要点在于：在向量空间的情形下我们可以求解；主要工具是基、矩阵以及大家反反复复练习过的矩阵算法。
So here's the point: but we can solve in the case of vector spaces, the main tools are bases, matrices, and matrix algorithms that you've all practiced ad nauseam.

92
00:28:20,383 --> 00:28:24,992
是的，它们实际上确实有用！
Yes, they are actually useful for something!

93
00:28:24,992 --> 00:28:50,320
那么让我们来看看我的具体含义。为此我想建立一些对应关系，建立一些对应词典：这里有若干对应关系。
So let's start looking at what I mean by that. In order to do that, I want to set up some correspondences, I want to set up some dictionaries here: so here are some correspondences.

94
00:28:50,320 --> 00:29:07,088
我想建立的第一个对应关系是我们在上一讲中以某种形式见过的，尽管当时未必完全明确——至少当时只在一个方向上明确指出过——但让我们复习一下，因为它非常重要。
The first correspondence I want to set up is one that we saw in some form in last lecture, although it wasn't necessarily made completely explicit—at least it was only made explicit in one direction—but let's review it because it's so important.

95
00:29:07,088 --> 00:29:39,735
我们在上一讲看到，如果 V 是域 F 上的n 维向量空间，那么基对应于某种事物：基对应于标准 n 维向量空间F^n 与V 之间的线性同构。
So we saw last lecture that if V is an n- dimensional vector space over a field F, then bases correspond to something: bases correspond to linear isomorphisms between the sort of canonical n-dimensional vector space F^n and V.

96
00:29:39,735 --> 00:30:14,871
在 V 的基与从 F^n 到 V 的线性同构之间存在一一满射对应（双射对应）。假设我有一组基，并且我们假设基是有序的——
There is a correspondence—a one-to-one onto correspondence—between bases of V and linear isomorphisms from F^n to V. So suppose I have a basis, and we're going to assume that our bases are ordered—

97
00:30:14,871 --> 00:30:31,942
也许我该顺便加个括号说明这些是有序基——假设我的基 B 由向量 v_1 到 v_n 组成。我们上次定义了一个同构：我们是如何定义的？
so maybe I'll just put parenthetically that these are ordered bases—so suppose I have my basis B which consists of vectors v_1 through v_n. We defined last time an isomorphism: how did we define it?

98
00:30:31,942 --> 00:30:36,799
有人记得吗？
Does anybody remember?

99
00:30:42,680 --> 00:31:03,959
对，完全正确。意译一下，并引入一点非标准的记号——书上没有，但对本讲的目的很有用：我们将定义一个与该基 B 相关的映射 \rho_B，从 F^n 到 V。它做什么呢？
Yes, exactly. Paraphrasing, and introducing a bit of notation which isn't standard—it's not in the book or anything, but it's going to be a useful notation for the purposes of this lecture: we're going to define something I'm going to call \rho_B associated to this basis B, going from F^n to V. And what will it do?

100
00:31:03,959 --> 00:31:24,667
它取列向量——我通常将 F^n 的元素写成列向量——取列向量 a_1 到 a_n 并将其映为线性组合 a_1v_1 + ... + a_n v_n。
Well, it'll take the column vector—I'll write for the most part elements of F^n as column vectors—you take the column vector a_1 through a_n and you map it to the sum a_1 v_1 plus a_n v_n.

101
00:31:24,667 --> 00:31:35,959
反方向该如何进行？假设我们有一个从 F^n 到 V 的线性同构：对应于它的基是什么？
How do we go in the other direction? Suppose we have a linear isomorphism from F^n to V: what's the basis that corresponds to it?

102
00:31:35,959 --> 00:31:48,351
对，请讲。
Yes, go ahead.

103
00:31:48,351 --> 00:31:50,895
是的，可以这样表述。
Yeah, that's one way of putting it.

104
00:31:50,895 --> 00:32:00,291
另一种不直接把 B 视为矩阵的表述方式——我们何不将其视为某种有序集——把你刚才所说的换种说法就是：如果我们有某个同构 \rho，
Another way of putting it, so that one doesn't make direct reference to B as being a matrix—why don't we think of this just being some sort of ordered set—

105
00:32:00,291 --> 00:32:21,154
我们将其映为有序集：\rho(1, 0, 0, 0)，然后是 \rho(0, 1, 0, 0)，一直到 \rho(0, 0, 1)。
another way of putting exactly what you just said is that if we have some \rho, we take it to the ordered set \rho of 1 0 0 0 and then \rho 0 1 0 0 and then onwards to 0 0 1.

106
00:32:21,154 --> 00:32:37,659
所以有F^n 的这组标准基，我们只需在标准基上计算 \rho 即可。这只是一种把所有东西翻译成标准基语言的方式。
So there's this standard basis of F^n, and we just evaluate \rho on that standard basis. So this is just a way of sort of translating everything into standard basis language.

107
00:32:37,659 --> 00:32:51,920
这一切的关键，之所以奏效的核心原因，恰恰在于 F^n 配备了一组非常便于操作的基，而给定的抽象向量空间未必配备；
The whole point of this, the whole point of why this works, is precisely that F^n comes equipped with a sort of easy-to-work-with basis, and a given abstract vector space doesn't necessarily;

108
00:32:51,920 --> 00:33:07,159
但通过在标准基与你在向量空间中能找到的基之间进行翻译，你就能切实开展计算工作了。好的。总而言之，为什么这一切成立？
but by translating between the sort of canonical basis and whatever bases you might be able to find for your vector space, you're able to actually get work done. Okay. So in a word, why is all of this true?

109
00:33:07,159 --> 00:33:24,548
这直接源于上次我们对基的诠释：给定向量空间中的每个向量都可以唯一地表示为基元素的线性组合。这只是对该性质的重新诠释。
Well, this just follows from the fact that the interpretation we gave to a basis last time is that every vector in the given vector space can be written uniquely as a linear combination of those basis elements. This is simply a reinterpretation of that.

110
00:33:24,548 --> 00:33:32,665
总之我建议大家复习上次的笔记以了解具体细节，但这直接由上次的内容得出。
So anyway I refer you to your notes from last time to review exactly what's going on, but this follows from what we saw last time.

111
00:33:32,665 --> 00:34:08,845
好的，我想考察的第二个对应关系是大家在初等线性代数中见过的：即标准向量空间 F^n 与F^m 之间的线性变换对应于矩阵：对应于域F 上的 m × n 矩阵。
Okay, the second correspondence I want to look at is something that you saw in basic linear algebra, and that is that linear transformations between our sort of standard vector spaces F^n and F^m, these correspond to matrices: these correspond to m by n matrices over the field F.

112
00:34:08,845 --> 00:34:31,159
为了确保大家清楚这里的符号，再引入一个记号：我将与线性变换 f: F^n → F^m 相关的矩阵记作方括号 [f]。[f] 长什么样？
So another piece of notation just to make sure that we're all clear on what's going on here: I will denote the matrix associated to a linear transformation from F^n to F^m as square brackets f. What does square bracket f look like?

113
00:34:31,159 --> 00:34:39,847
用大家以前学过的语言来说，这就是关于两空间标准基的矩阵。
Well, maybe in the language you saw before, this is the matrix associated to this with respect to the standard bases on these things.

114
00:34:39,847 --> 00:35:06,185
那正是列向量形如 f(1, 0, ...)构成的矩阵，这里的每一列都是完整的列向量，所以你要把它视为一个矩阵，这不仅仅是一个 1，而是表示整整一列，然后我在所有的标准基元素上依次求值，一直到最后一列。
Well, that's just the matrix that looks like f of 1 0 dot dot dot, and so this is an entire column here, so you have to think of this as being a matrix, so this isn't a one, this is just saying that this is an entire column, and then I just evaluate on all of the standard basis elements all the way to the end.

115
00:35:06,185 --> 00:35:31,342
大家应该对反方向的操作很熟悉：我取一个矩阵 A，由此得到从 F^n 到 F^m 的线性变换，即将 F^n 中的向量 v 映为矩阵乘积 Av。
And I mean this should be pretty familiar, that this works going in the other direction: I take a matrix A, and from it I get a linear transformation from F^n to F^m by mapping a vector v in F^n to its matrix multiple by A.

116
00:35:31,342 --> 00:35:34,752
这正是我们以前学过的标准内容。
So this is just the standard thing we saw before.

117
00:35:34,752 --> 00:35:47,480
关于这个对应关系最重要的性质之一是：它保持了两侧大家所学过的所有自然运算。
Now one of the most important things about this correspondence is that it preserves the sorts of natural operations that you learned on both sides of that.

118
00:35:47,480 --> 00:36:12,380
在左侧线性变换这边，大家知道可以做线性变换的加法、数乘以及复合；而关键在于方括号操作保持了这些运算。简言之：[c_1 f_1 + c_2 f_2] 等于 c_1 方括号[f_1] + c_2 [f_2]。
So on the side of the linear transformations here, you know that you can add linear transformations, and you can scalar multiply, and you can compose; and the point is that that's preserved by this taking of brackets. So in brief: c_1 f_1 plus c_2 f_2 equal c_1 bracket f_1 plus c_2 bracket f_2.

119
00:36:12,380 --> 00:36:23,659
如果取相应的矩阵，它保持了所有这类线性结构；并且此外，如果复合 f_1 与 f_2，那正好对应于矩阵乘法。
If I take the matrices associated to these things, it preserves all this sort of structure, and moreover, if I compose f_1 and f_2, well that just corresponds to matrix multiplication.

120
00:36:23,659 --> 00:36:36,390
这极为重要，因为我们非常清楚如何做矩阵乘法，我们知道如何以简单、高效的算法完成这些操作。这是一种翻译成矩阵语言的方式。
This is very important because we know exactly how to do matrix multiplication, we know how to do all these things in a very simple, efficient, algorithmic way. So this is a way of just translating into the language of matrices.

121
00:36:36,390 --> 00:37:01,839
那么让我们把这些内容结合起来，把这两个对应关系结合起来：如果把对应关系 1 和 2 结合在一起，会得到什么？
So let's sort of put these things together, put these two correspondences together: so if I take correspondences 1 and 2 and I put them together, what do I get?

122
00:37:01,839 --> 00:37:21,915
给定从 V 到 V' 的某个线性变换——这只是某个线性变换，假设它们的维数分别为 n 和 m，并且我们为它们配备基 B 和 B'。
Given some linear transformation from say V to V'—this is just some linear transformation, and let's assume that this thing has dimension n and m, and let's just equip these things with bases B and B'.

123
00:37:21,915 --> 00:37:36,578
这些是维数为 n 和 m 的有限维向量空间，我为它们配备基 B 和 B'。我们知道总能给向量空间配备一组基——至少我们在有限维情形下证明了这一点。
So these are these finite- dimensional vector spaces of dimension n and m, and I equip them with these bases B and B', we know we can always equip a vector space with a basis—at least we showed that in the finite-dimensional case.

124
00:37:36,578 --> 00:37:54,119
还有一个更一般的证明，适用于最一般的向量空间理论（允许无限维向量空间），但那需要用到一点集合论以及备受争议的选择公理。
There is a proof that's more general that works in sort of the most general version of the theory of vector spaces where you allow infinite-dimensional vector spaces, but that requires a little set theory and the controversial axiom of choice.

125
00:37:54,119 --> 00:37:58,680
那么给定这些之后我们做什么？
So given this thing, what do we do?

126
00:37:58,680 --> 00:38:26,034
我们有映射 f 关于基 B 和 B' 的矩阵。我们如何定义它？让我们给它一个记号：[f]_{B, B'}。这个矩阵就是 \rho_{B'}^{-1} ∘ f ∘ \rho_B。
Well, we have the matrix of f with respect to B and B'. How do we define this? Well, let's just give it a notation: f B B'. This thing is \rho_{B'}^{-1} f \rho_B.

127
00:38:26,034 --> 00:38:28,435
为什么这样合理？
Why does this make sense?

128
00:38:28,435 --> 00:38:44,891
我们定义的 \rho_B 把形如标准向量空间 F^n 映到我们所处的向量空间 V；接着 f 把向量空间 V 映到向量空间 V' 中；
Well, we defined \rho_B so that it takes this, you know, standard vector space, these things of the form F^n, to the vector space we're working in, V. Then f takes the vector space we're working in, V,

129
00:38:44,891 --> 00:39:06,218
然后 \rho_{B'}^{-1} 把抽象向量空间 V' 翻译回来，利用基 B' 在标准向量空间 F^m 中给出一个元素。这就是 f 关于基 B 和 B' 的矩阵。
to something in the vector space V', then \rho_{B'}^{-1} translates back out of the abstract language of these vector spaces V' and gives you something in this sort of canonical vector space F^m using this basis B'. So it's the matrix of f with respect to B and B'.

130
00:39:06,218 --> 00:39:56,323
另一种显式的看待方式是：具体来说，如果 B 是 {v_1, ..., v_n} 且 B' 是 {w_1, ..., w_m}，那么给定任意 v_j，我们知道其像可以唯一地写成基 B' 中元素的线性组合。这是基的定义性特征。
Another sort of explicit way of looking at this is: explicitly, if B is v_1 through v_n and B' is, say, w_1 through w_m, then well, given any of these v_j's, we know that we can write its image uniquely as a linear combination of things in this basis B'. That was this defining characteristic of bases.

131
00:39:56,323 --> 00:40:19,000
因此对每个 j（j 取遍 1 到 n），它看起来就是求和：∑_{i=1}^m a_{ij} w_i，其中 a_{ij} 为某些标量。那么矩阵 [f]_{B, B'} 是什么呢？
So this thing looks like just the sum: for each of these j's (j is just ranging over 1 through n), this looks like the sum i = 1 to m a_i j w_i for some scalars a_i j. So what is this thing, f B B'?

132
00:40:19,000 --> 00:40:27,406
它正是由这些数构成的矩阵 (a_{ij})，从该定义出发极易验证。
Well, it's just this matrix made up of these numbers, and it's a very easy verification from this definition.

133
00:40:27,406 --> 00:40:47,740
这个定义只是一种精妙且便于操作的方式，用以引出关于基 B 和 B' 矩阵的这种更具计算性的表述。再次说明这一点：让我们来做个总结。
This definition is just a sort of fancy and easy-to-work-with way of introducing this more computational way of referring to the matrix with respect to B and B Prime.

134
00:40:47,740 --> 00:41:17,341
首先，这建立了一个非常漂亮的对应关系；它允许我们断言 Hom(V, V')——即从 V 到 V' 的所有线性变换的集合——实际上具有向量空间结构，我们稍后就会看到这一点。
And again this sort of thing: so let's just actually summarize this. First of all, this sets up a very, very nice correspondence; this thing allows us to say that Hom(V, V')—by which I mean the set of linear transformations from V to V'—this thing in fact has a vector space structure on it, and that's something we're going to sort of see in a minute.

135
00:41:17,341 --> 00:41:34,885
在选定基之后，它实际上与域 F 上的m × n 矩阵空间 M_{m×n}(F) 本质相同，严格同构。
This thing is actually, given a choice of bases, essentially the same thing, or exactly isomorphic to, but in light of this particular choice, the m by n matrices over F.

136
00:41:34,885 --> 00:41:51,705
这只是重申我们刚才所讲的，但我刚才想强调的是它具有优良的附加结构：我可以将线性变换空间Hom(V, V') 中的元素相加、数乘以及进行复合。
This is just restating what we stated over here, but what I was just saying is that this thing has this nice sort of additional structure on it: I can add things in the set of linear transformations from V to V', I can scalar multiply them, and I can compose them.

137
00:41:51,705 --> 00:42:08,280
关键在于：我们见过的第二个对应关系（对应关系 II）保持了该结构，这蕴含了这里的对应关系 III 也同样保持该结构。
And the point is that the fact that the correspondence that we saw—the second correspondence we saw, the Roman numeral II correspondence—preserved that structure implies that this Roman numeral III correspondence also preserves that structure.

138
00:42:08,280 --> 00:42:29,680
显式地写出来就是：[c_1 f_1 + c_2 f_2]_{B, B'} 等于 c_1 [f_1]_{B, B'}+ c_2 [f_2]_{B, B'}。
So put explicitly: c_1 f_1 plus c_2 f_2 with respect to some B and B' is equal to c_1 f_1 with respect to B and B' plus c_2 f_2 to B B'.

139
00:42:29,680 --> 00:42:56,354
此外，如果再次有 f: V → V' 以及 g: V' → V''，并且同样为它们配备基 B、B' 和 B''，那么正如你所期望的那样，复合结构也同样得以保持——这再次由我们之前所见的结果得出。
Now moreover, if I have again f: V -> V' and g from V' to V'', and, you know, again I sort of equip these things with bases B, B', and B'', then exactly the sort of composition structure that you expect to be preserved is preserved—again this just sort of follows from what we saw before.

140
00:42:56,354 --> 00:43:08,779
复合映射 g ∘ f 是从 V 到 V''——所以我最好关于基 B 和 B'' 来取矩阵。
So g compose f—so g compose f goes from V to V''— so I better take this with respect to bases B and B Double Prime.

141
00:43:08,779 --> 00:43:29,440
因此关于 B 和 B'' 的矩阵，正好等于矩阵 [g]_{B', B''} 与 [f]_{B, B'} 的乘积：[g ∘ f] = [g][f]。这正是你所期望的复合形式。
So B and B Double Prime, well, this thing just looks like the matrix multiple of g with respect to B' and B'' with f with respect to B and B'. It's just exactly the sort of composition that you expect.

142
00:43:29,440 --> 00:43:45,815
这很清楚吧？有什么问题吗？请问，您在 g 周围写的方括号，我应该理解为……实现 g 作用的矩阵？
Is that pretty clear? Are there any questions? Yes, the box that you've written around g, I should read that to myself as the linear as the matrix that does what g does?

143
00:43:45,815 --> 00:44:09,908
是的！你应该把它理解为完全按照这套公式定义的矩阵，只需将 f 换成 g，并将标量替换为适用于 g 的标量；或者直接用我们之前的定义：即 \rho_{B''}^{-1} ∘ g ∘ \rho_{B'}。
Yeah! So what you should do is think of this alternatively as being the thing defined, the matrix defined by exactly this set of formulas, but replacing f with g and replacing these scalars with the ones that work for g; or just the thing that we defined before: this is \rho_{B''}^{-1} g \rho_{B'}.

144
00:44:09,908 --> 00:44:31,720
这个映射从维数为 dim(V') 的标准向量空间出发，映到维数为 dim(V'') 的标准向量空间，而我们知道如何为它写出矩阵。清楚了吗？很好。
This thing goes from the canonical vector space of dimension the dimension of V' to the canonical vector space of dimension the dimension of V'', and we know how to write matrices for that. Is that clear? Cool.

145
00:44:31,720 --> 00:44:45,453
好的，我们保持了结构，拥有了所有这些优良的性质。
Okay, so we preserve the structure, we have all these great properties.

146
00:44:45,453 --> 00:44:52,760
如果我们想要更换基该怎么办？基并不是正则（唯一的），给定的向量空间有许许多多的基。
What if we want to change bases? I mean, there's nothing canonical about a basis; there are lots and lots of bases for a given vector space.

147
00:44:52,760 --> 00:45:05,041
有时根据实际应用你需要在不同的基下工作；有时存在比你最初使用的基更方便的基。
Sometimes you need to work in different vector in different bases according to the applications; sometimes there are more convenient bases than the one that you started working with.

148
00:45:05,041 --> 00:45:29,603
因此假设在计算过程中你需要变换基：该怎么做？这同样只是初等线性代数内容的升级版；只是把任意域上抽象向量空间理论的形式套用在大家已经学过的理论上。
So suppose in the middle of your calculations you need to start changing bases: how do you do this? Well, again this is just a souped-up version of exactly what you saw in basic linear algebra; this is just putting all the trappings of this theory of abstract vector spaces over an arbitrary field on a theory that you've already seen.

149
00:45:29,603 --> 00:45:55,720
基变换：假设我们有空间 V，具有两组基 B_1 和 B_2；我们有域 F 上的向量空间 V'，具有两组基 B_1' 和 B_2'。
So change of bases: so suppose we have V, and it has bases B_1 and B_2, and we have vector space V' over F, and it has bases B_1' and B_2'.

150
00:45:56,960 --> 00:46:24,261
让我们显式写出 f 在第二组基下的矩阵：假设你将其写为关于 B_2 和 B_2' 的矩阵：我们将其定义为 \rho_{B_2'}^{-1} ∘ f ∘ \rho_{B_2}，对吧？
Well, let's just sort of write out explicitly what f is in terms of the second vector space: so suppose you write this in terms of B_2, B_2': well, we define this as being \rho_{B_2'}^{-1} f \rho_{B_2}, right?

151
00:46:24,261 --> 00:46:40,650
但我总是可以在这里插入 \rho_{B_1'} \rho_{B_1'}^{-1}——那只是恒等映射，因此我完全可以把它插入这里——并且我也能在另一边做同样的事。
But I can always just sort of insert here, say, \rho_{B_1'} \rho_{B_1'}^{-1}—that's just the identity map, so I'm certainly allowed to insert it here—and I can do the same sort of thing over here.

152
00:46:40,650 --> 00:47:05,175
让我完全显式地写出来：我可以将其重写为 (\rho_{B_2'}^{-1} \rho_{B_1'}) 乘上(\rho_{B_1'}^{-1} f \rho_{B_1}) \rho_{B_1}^{-1}—
So let me just write that out completely explicitly: I can rewrite this as \rho_{B_2'}^{-1} \rho_{B_1'} times \rho B_1' inverse f \rho_{B_1} \rho_{B_1}^{-1}—this thing again is the identity, so I'm just allowed to insert it wherever I want,

153
00:47:05,175 --> 00:47:24,633
—这项同样是恒等映射，所以我可以随意插入，只要它是相应向量空间上的恒等映射即可，而它确实是——再乘上 \rho_{B_2}。由于取矩阵的复合保持性质，这种取括号操作——大家知道，
as long as it's the identity on the right vector space, and it certainly is—\rho_{B_2}. So I can, because of the sort of composition property of this taking matrices, this sort of bracketing operation—

154
00:47:24,633 --> 00:47:50,211
这种方括号操作意味着取矩阵——我们之前看到它保持复合，所以我可以将其重写为 (\rho_{B_2'}^{-1} \rho_{B_1'}) 乘上 (\rho_{B_1'}^{-1}f \rho_{B_1}) 再乘上
so this bracketing operation, you know, you just have to think: okay, that means take the matrix—well, we saw before that it preserves composition, so I could rewrite this as \rho_{B_2'}^{-1} \rho_{B_1'} times

155
00:47:50,211 --> 00:47:54,251
(\rho_{B_1}^{-1} \rho_{B_2})。
\rho_{B_1}' inverse f \rho_{B_1} times \rho_{B_1}^{-1} \rho_{B_2}.

156
00:47:54,251 --> 00:47:57,800
我为什么要这么做？
Why did I do this?

157
00:48:00,040 --> 00:48:08,948
因为夹在中间的正是 f 关于基 B_1 和 B_1' 的矩阵！
Well, stuck in the middle here is f with respect to the bases B_1' and B_1.

158
00:48:08,948 --> 00:48:43,698
这正好等于 (\rho_{B_2'}^{-1}\rho_{B_1'}) 乘以 [f]_{B_1, B_1'} 乘以 (\rho_{B_1}^{-1} \rho_{B_2})。请注意夹在两侧的式子看起来非常相似。
This thing is exactly equal to \rho_{B_1}—sorry, B_2 inverse \rho B_1 times f with respect to B_1' and B_1 times \rho_{B_1}^{-1} \rho_{B_2}. And notice the things on either side of this look very, very similar.

159
00:48:43,698 --> 00:49:00,343
是的，带撇号的肯定在左边，谢谢，完全正确！因此对于形如这样的矩阵，自然称为基变换矩阵。
Yeah, I mean the primes should certainly be on the left, thank you, absolutely! So things that look like this, it makes sense to call change of basis matrices.

160
00:49:00,343 --> 00:49:33,359
我们给它这个称谓：把形如 \rho_{B_1}^{-1} \rho_{B_2} 的矩阵称为基变换矩阵。事实上在给定 B_1 和 B_2 后，它是唯一的。
So let's just give it that moniker: so call something of the form \rho_{B_1}^{-1} \rho_{B_2} the change of basis matrix for—a change of basis matrix. In fact it's unique given B_2 and B_1.

161
00:49:36,919 --> 00:49:53,720
但这稍微有点一般化。大家可能见过本质相同的构造，但局限在 V 与 V' 是同一个空间的特例中。
But now this is a bit general. You've probably seen this construction in an essentially identical form, but in the special case where V and V' are the same.

162
00:49:53,720 --> 00:50:10,399
如果 V = V'，那么我可以将其重写为 [f]_{B_2, B_2}；于是我们只有两组基 B_1, B_2，它们同时是两边的基。
So if V equals V', then, well, I can just rewrite this as B_2 B_2, so I again I just have B_1 B_2, and so now these are bases for both V and V',

163
00:50:10,399 --> 00:50:23,441
这个式子就变成了 (\rho_{B_1}^{-1} \rho_{B_2})^{-1}因为那等于 \rho_{B_2}^{-1} \rho_{B_1}，
this thing just looks like \rho_{B_1}^{-1} \rho_{B_2} all inverse, because that looks like \rho_{B_2}^{-1} \rho_{B_1},

164
00:50:23,441 --> 00:50:39,800
我可以去掉撇号因为处理的是同一空间，乘以 [f]_{B_1, B_1}再乘以 (\rho_{B_1}^{-1} \rho_{B_2})。
and I could remove the primes here because I'm just taking this same vector space, times f with respect to B_1 and B_1 times \rho_{B_1}^{-1} \rho_{B_2}.

165
00:50:39,800 --> 00:50:56,295
这正是相似矩阵的概念：这是形如 P^{-1}[f]_{B_1, B_1} P（即 P^{-1} [f] P）的形式，其中 P 正是该基变换矩阵。
So this is just the the idea of similar matrices: this is something of the form P f B_1 B_1 P inverse, rather f B_1 B_1 P, where P is exactly this change of basis matrix.

166
00:50:56,295 --> 00:51:09,640
现在退回到刚才的一般构造，为了便于计算，让我们显式写出那个矩阵是什么。
Now stepping back to the general construction for just a second, let's just explicitly write down, for sort of calculation purposes, what that thing is.

167
00:51:09,640 --> 00:51:33,200
如果 B_1 可以写成{v_1, ..., v_n}，B_2 写成 {w_1, ..., w_n}，那么 \rho_{B_1}^{-1} \rho_{B_2} 正是矩阵 c_{ij}，
Well, if I have B_1 and I can write it as v_1 through v_n, and I have B_2 and I write it as w_1 through w_n, then \rho_{B_1}^{-1} \rho_{B_2} is just the matrix c_i j,

168
00:51:33,200 --> 00:51:55,760
其中我再次利用基的定义性质，将每个元素 w_j 写成 v_i 的线性组合，这显然是可以做到的：w_j = ∑_{i=1}^n c_{ij} v_i，其中 i 取遍 1 到 n。
where I again use this sort of defining property of bases to write each element w_j as a linear combination of the—which I can certainly do: so this is i ranging over 1 to n.

169
00:51:57,359 --> 00:52:06,480
在实际计算时，这就是你所做的事。
To calculate, this is what you do.

170
00:52:06,480 --> 00:52:24,470
如果思考一下我们写在这里的式子，在群论中我们实际上给这种事物起了个不同的名字：在初等线代中你称其为相似矩阵理论，但在群论中这就是矩阵的共轭。
So if I just sort of think about this kind of thing that we've written down here, we've actually given this sort of thing a name: I mean, in basic linear algebra you call this like the theory of similar matrices, but so far in group theory we've given this a different name: that's conjugation of matrices.

171
00:52:24,470 --> 00:52:37,089
因此大家在这门课中需要开始做的，就是逐渐摆脱“相似矩阵”这种语言，转向群论语言：将其称为共轭。
So what you have to start doing is, in the—you know, in this sort of course you want to start moving away from that language of like similar matrices and to the language of group theory: so you would talk about this as being conjugacy.

172
00:52:37,089 --> 00:52:44,187
事实上这完全合情合理，因为我们确实有一个在其内部进行这种共轭运算的群。
And in fact this totally makes sense because we actually have a group in which we're doing this conjugation.

173
00:52:44,187 --> 00:53:14,280
让我把它明确讲出来：再次从某个向量空间 V 出发——V 为任意向量空间——那么我们定义 GL(V) 为从 V 到 V 的所有线性同构构成的集合。
Let me make that explicit: so again, let's just start with some vector space V—so V is just some vector space—well, then we define GL(V) to be the set of linear isomorphisms from V to V.

174
00:53:14,280 --> 00:53:29,409
这类似于群的自同构群 Aut(G)，只不过我们提出了额外的要求：不仅要求它是群同构，还要求它保持数乘。
So this is sort of the analog of the automorphism group of a group, except that we demand something additional: we demand not only that this thing be a group isomorphism, but that it preserve the scalar multiplication.

175
00:53:29,409 --> 00:53:55,129
因此它们是线性同构，但特别地，你可以将其视为 V（仅看作加法群时）的自同构群的子群。换句话说，它们就是从 V 到 V 的可逆线性变换。
So these are linear isomorphisms, but in particular you can think of this as being some subgroup of the automorphism group of V just viewed as a group. So put another way, these are just the invertible linear transformations from V to V.

176
00:53:55,129 --> 00:54:06,200
或者用我们见过多次的语言来说：我们把 Z/nZ 中的可逆元称作什么？
Or using a language that we've seen several times: what did we call the invertible elements of Z/nZ?

177
00:54:07,950 --> 00:54:19,604
没错，(Z/nZ)^×！所以在我们目前引入的记号下，完全可以将其记作 Hom(V, V)^×。
Exactly, (Z/nZ)^\times! So it actually makes sense, given the notation we've introduced so far, to call this Hom(V, V)^\times.

178
00:54:19,604 --> 00:54:34,640
现在记住我们刚才展示的核心要点：Hom(V, V) 可以翻译成一种新的语言：在选定基之后，翻译成矩阵的语言。
Now remember the whole point of what we were just showing is that Hom(V, V) we can sort of translate into a new language: the language of matrices, given a choice of basis.

179
00:54:36,919 --> 00:55:12,608
因此给定 V 的一组基，我们刚才看到可以将其同构地重写为 M_{n×n}(F) 中的可逆矩阵集合，其中 n 是 V 的维数。
So given a basis B of V, we just saw we can rewrite this isomorphically as the set of invertible matrices in, uh, in M_{n \times n}(F), where n is the dimension of V.

180
00:55:12,608 --> 00:55:23,104
这个集合叫什么？可逆矩阵的集合叫什么？GL_n(F)！
What is this thing called? What is the set of invertible matrices? GL_n(F)!

181
00:55:23,104 --> 00:55:37,799
所以思路在于：我们有抽象的对象 GL(V)，但当我们需要处理它时，用矩阵来工作要方便得多，因为你可以切实地用矩阵进行计算，
So the idea is that we have this abstract thing GL(V), but when we need to work with it, it's much more convenient to work with matrices, because you can actually do calculation with matrices;

182
00:55:37,799 --> 00:55:51,844
并且在选定基后很容易做到这一点：你得到了与 GL_n(F) 的诱导同构，因此现在处理任何你想做的事都变得非常简单。
and given a choice of basis, you know, you can easily do this: you have an induced isomorphism rather with GL_n(F), and so it now becomes very easy to do whatever you want.

183
00:55:51,844 --> 00:55:58,109
好的，总体要点在于你可以建立这种词典。
Okay, the general point here is that you can set up this sort of dictionary.

184
00:55:58,109 --> 00:56:16,599
最后还有一个思考题留给大家思考：在这种语言中，在这样的翻译下，一个线性变换的像在矩阵语言中对应于什么？
Just one last question to to feed your thought: in this language, in this sort of translation, what is the image of a linear transformation in terms of matrices?

185
00:56:16,599 --> 00:56:28,760
对，列空间，完全正确！在这一词典下，像就等同于列空间；而我们知道如何求矩阵的列空间。
Yes, the column space, exactly! The image under this sort of dictionary is the same thing as the column space; we know how to find the column space of a matrix.

186
00:56:28,760 --> 00:56:36,167
因此给定一个抽象向量空间，我们现在有了一套算法来求给定线性变换的像。
So given an abstract vector space, we now have an algorithm for finding the image of a given linear transformation.

187
00:56:36,167 --> 00:56:47,507
同样的道理也适用于核，因为你可以求矩阵的零空间（解空间），而在该词典下那恰好就是核。
The same thing applies to the kernel, because you can find the null space of a matrix, and that thing under this dictionary is precisely the kernel.

188
00:56:47,507 --> 00:56:51,760
这些就留给大家课后思考。
So that's just food for thought.
